# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 2f (partner opens 1C).
title: Partner opens 1♣: show diamonds, then bid game
id: L02-20
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.6
student: S
board: 20
dealer: W
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  A84    K63    K4     QJT86
  E  T5     J875   J76    A742
  S  KJ3    AQT    Q983   K95
  W  Q9762  942    AT52   3

auction:
  W Pass
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 1D*    = 6+ points, four or more diamonds
     key: 15 HCP, balanced, with four diamonds. Show your suit at the one level; partner will bid again.
     not 2NT: 2NT shows 12-14. Did you count 15?
     not 2C: Raising shows 6-9, and you have more. Can you show your diamonds first?
     not 3NT: A jump to 3NT isn't in our system. Start with 1♦.
     not *: With four diamonds, which response shows them at the one level?
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = A balanced minimum, 13-14
  E Pass
  S 3NT*   = Game
     key: Partner showed 13-14. With your 15, your side has 28 or more: bid game.
     not Pass: Partner showed 13-14. With your 15, is there enough for game?
     not 2NT: 2NT invites. With 28 or more between you, do you need partner's help to decide?
  W Pass
  N Pass
  E Pass

auction recap:
  1♦ showed four diamonds and 6+ points, and partner had to bid again. His
  1NT showed a balanced minimum. 15 plus 13-14 is 28 or more, so you bid
  game. North is declarer, because he bid no-trump first, and so East will
  lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E H5  S HQ  W H2  N H3
  2   S CK  W C3  N C6  E CA
      note: Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A, then run the clubs. Dummy's ♣K first, the high card from the short side.
  3   E H7  S HA  W H4  N H6
  4   S D3  W D2  N DK  E D6
      note: A diamond to declarer's king.
  5   N S4  E S5  S SJ  W SQ
      note: A spade toward dummy's ♠KJ.
  6   W H9  N HK  E H8  S HT
  7   N CQ  E C2  S C5  W S2
      note: Now run the clubs.
  8   N CJ  E C4  S C9  W S6
      note: Keep going.
  9   N CT  E C7  S D8  W D5
      note: And again.
  10  N C8  E ST  S D9  W S7
      note: The last club.
  11  N SA  E D7  S S3  W S9
      note: The ♠A.
  12  N S8  E HJ  S SK  W DT
      note: A spade to dummy's king.
  13  S DQ  W DA  N D4  E DJ
      note: West's ♦A takes the last trick. 10 tricks: 3NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A and run the clubs.

  3NT made with an overtrick. Your 1♦ kept the auction low while partner
  described his hand, and then you knew enough to bid game.
